WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:05.040
Speaker 1: Let's go next to Mo from West Virginia.

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:07.029
Mo from West Virginia, welcome.

00:00:07.029 --> 00:00:08.670
What's on your mind today, sir?

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:10.429
Speaker 3: Hi, David.

00:00:10.429 --> 00:00:14.880
I just wanted to ask you might be a two part
question.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:15.880
Sure.

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:20.529
One is that I see you on mostly left wing
media.

00:00:20.529 --> 00:00:25.990
Corporate media does is to where they say
that Trump and DeSantis are too far to the

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:30.970
right when it comes to policies and positions
to gain traction with independents.

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:32.800
They're turning off independents.

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:38.719
Well, as we all have seen in the past, before
the primaries come first.

00:00:38.719 --> 00:00:44.579
So obviously they're going to go for the right
wingers to win their primaries.

00:00:44.579 --> 00:00:45.579
Yes.

00:00:45.579 --> 00:00:51.890
After the primaries, there's a lot of shift
in their policies and positions to gain back

00:00:51.890 --> 00:00:54.170
some momentum with independents.

00:00:54.170 --> 00:01:01.039
Do you see anyone in the media actually like
paying attention to that?

00:01:01.039 --> 00:01:03.760
Is that a thing that could happen with DeSantis
or Trump?

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:09.869
Speaker 1: I think it'll happen to a degree
with both of them if they win the primary,

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:13.560
but we'll all realize it's not genuine.

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:20.610
And also, I think right now the environment
is such that they all know they need to play

00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:26.460
to this extreme MAGA, right, that, remember,
doesn't really even care about policy.

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:32.070
They care about culture issues, fighting Wokeness,
owning the libs, and some very vague, you

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:34.860
know, I'll build a wall or whatever.

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:40.060
I actually think there's more risk right now
to the Republican candidate of playing to

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:44.970
the middle in the general that they will they
will turn off some of those extreme voters.

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:50.310
So I think to some degree, whoever wins the
Republican primary will make a slight play

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:51.310
to the middle.

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:56.450
I think it won't be as much as we often see
because it's really risky and I think it will

00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:58.770
be transparently disingenuous.

00:01:58.770 --> 00:02:01.990
Speaker 3: Where's the risk, though?

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:06.750
Because once they win the primary there, that
you're a Republican guy, so the risk will

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:07.750
get beat.

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:12.590
Speaker 1: You have to remember right now
MAGA is made up of the traditional Republican

00:02:12.590 --> 00:02:19.060
electorate, plus people who only ever started
following politics because of Trump.

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:25.590
Many of those people, if they become disaffected
with whoever it is, Trump, DeSantis, whatever,

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:29.170
they will stay home and then it'll really
hurt your ability to win.

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:32.920
That's the risk that they will just say, This
wasn't what I thought I was getting.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:34.030
I'm staying home.

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:35.510
Screw them.

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:41.420
They are willing to do that because they are
not traditional historical voters that vote

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:42.530
every election.

00:02:42.530 --> 00:02:46.930
And so those folks are much more open to simply
not voting at all.

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:53.700
Speaker 3: I guess that's true, but that's
mostly I see there as a bigger risk with the

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:57.080
scientists than Trump, because Trump Trump
has that voter base.

00:02:57.080 --> 00:02:59.890
Like I feel like even DeSantis voters.

00:02:59.890 --> 00:03:04.840
If Trump becomes the winner of the primary,
they'll still vote for Trump just because

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:06.640
he's the Republican.

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:09.870
They're not going to vote Democrat in any
situation.

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:11.440
They mostly will get votes.

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:12.440
Speaker 1: You're right.

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:13.840
They mostly will.

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:19.390
But this is a very unusual situation where
at this point, Trump pretending to pander

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:24.140
to the middle a little bit is not going to
really win him any votes because it will be

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:29.360
so obviously disingenuous and it has the risk
of turning off some of his supporters.

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:34.650
I think the most likely outcome is Trump just
doesn't do it and he doesn't play to the middle

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:35.650
at all.

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:38.439
Speaker 3: Trump doesn't.

00:03:38.439 --> 00:03:39.439
Yes.

00:03:39.439 --> 00:03:41.950
Speaker 1: That's my guess.

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:43.110
That's my prediction.

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:49.790
Speaker 3: Do you see any specific policies
that you think he would be more likely to

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:54.519
flip on or positions he takes right now that
you would be willing to give up?

00:03:54.519 --> 00:03:56.160
Speaker 1: I really don't.

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:58.870
And remember, he barely takes any policy positions.

00:03:58.870 --> 00:04:01.890
I mean, he's running a social issues anti-woke.

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:03.340
I won in 2020.

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:04.550
They treated me unfairly.

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:07.200
Biden's a marxist type of campaign.

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:11.690
It's already pretty devoid of policy, so there's
not that much policy he even could flip on.

00:04:11.690 --> 00:04:12.840
Speaker 3: Right.

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:14.900
There's nothing like he doesn't give out specifics.

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:18.229
And I mean, I.
Speaker 1: Guess he said he would do anything.

00:04:18.229 --> 00:04:21.540
He was going to build tent cities and force
homeless people in there.

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:22.790
Maybe he'll cancel that plan.

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:23.790
I don't know.

00:04:23.790 --> 00:04:24.790
Speaker 3: Right.

00:04:24.790 --> 00:04:28.450
But like his position on Ukraine, where he
was asked in the town hall, like, would you

00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:30.000
stop supporting Ukraine?

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.320
Who do you want to win the war?

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:34.210
He's is not taking a side.

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:39.540
He kind of just made an appeal to emotion
saying he just wanted people to stop dying.

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:40.729
Exactly right.

00:04:40.729 --> 00:04:43.850
Do you see him leaning one way or another
more?

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:47.030
Speaker 1: I'm really not sure.

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:53.160
You know, it's it's just it's a fool's errand
to try to predict exactly which way Trump

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:54.350
will lean on these issues.

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:59.139
It'll be whatever he thinks will benefit him
at the time based on what's being said on

00:04:59.139 --> 00:05:03.810
Fox News and what people around him are saying,
it's it's not even worth taking a guess.

00:05:03.810 --> 00:05:04.920
I just have no idea.

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:09.610
Speaker 3: So you'll think he'll stick to
whatever people around him are saying more?

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:11.800
Yeah, even if they're not like that.

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:13.510
He really is like advisers.

00:05:13.510 --> 00:05:15.280
On helping him win the election, per se.

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:17.030
Speaker 1: That's what he said historically.

00:05:17.030 --> 00:05:18.290
Speaker 3: Okay.

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:19.290
Well.

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:23.319
Speaker 1: All right, my friend, I appreciate
Mo from West Virginia.

00:05:23.319 --> 00:05:24.870
Great to hear from you.

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:28.980
Let's take a very quick break and then we'll
take more calls.

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:40.389
So hang on if you're waiting to talk to me.

